;; stratified negation inside a RECURSIVE rule (docs/incremental.md 0.8):
;; reachability that avoids blocked nodes.  The negated relation (blocked)
;; is closed below the reach SCC, so the absent probe rides every
;; delta-driven version of the recursive rule against a stable full index.
table (edge int int)
table (blocked int)
table (reach int int)

rule
(edge 1 2) (edge 2 3) (edge 3 4) (edge 2 5) (edge 5 6)
(blocked 3)

rule
(edge X Y)
~(blocked Y)
-->
(reach X Y)

rule
(reach X Y)
(edge Y Z)
~(blocked Z)
-->
(reach X Z)
